BLOCK 5 -- cross-validation against the M7 engine (m7_price.BlockChain)
======================================================================================
    [ok ] M7's two-ladder engine agrees with the enclosure at every mode  max difference 1.313e-16 over h = 1..8
    [ok ] M7's numerical stationary vector is accurate here -- but it is not certified  ||pi_exact - pi_numeric||_1 = 6.106e-16

======================================================================================
BLOCK 6 -- why circulations: the alternative needs pi, and pi resists certification
======================================================================================
    Parametrised by q, the stationary vector is a Perron eigenvector and a rigorous
    Phi needs ||pi - pi~||_1, which enters Phi linearly (|Phi~ - sum pi~ W| <= ||pi-pi~||_1
    since |W| <= 1).  The cheap route to that is the residual bound
    ||pi - pi~||_1 <= ||pi~ P^k - pi~||_1 / (1 - tau(P^k)) with the Dobrushin coefficient
    tau(P^k) <= 1 - sum_u min_b P^k(b,u).  Measured at L = 8:

    chain                                h(mu)     tau(P^8)    tau(P^16)    tau(P^32)    tau(P^64)
    random word, uniform 1/20           0.6688    6.521e-01    1.080e-02    1.111e-06    1.965e-14
    random word, uniform 1e-5           0.6660    7.071e-01    1.309e-02    1.891e-06    5.462e-14
    periodic 110100, uniform 1/20       0.0388    9.988e-01    9.940e-01    9.842e-01    9.650e-01
    periodic 110100, uniform 1/1000     0.0008    1.000e+00    9.999e-01    9.997e-01    9.993e-01
    [ok ] the residual route works for a high-entropy chain  tau(P^32) = 1.11e-06, so the amplification is 1.000001
    [ok ] and COLLAPSES for a low-entropy one -- exactly the witnesses Route 4 may need  tau(P^64) = 0.9993, amplification 1476x
    A circulation needs none of this: conservation IS stationarity, so pi is read off
    the parameters as an exact rational.  Cost of certifying pi: zero, at every entropy.

